---
title: "Acme Connection"
description: "AcmeConnection registers events without the on_ prefix; an events table names them."
---

## Configuration

```python
from pipecat.services.acme.connection import AcmeConnection
```

### AcmeConnection

<ParamField path="user" type="str" required>
  User part of the address.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="domain" type="str" required>
  Registration domain.
</ParamField>

<ParamField path="password" type="str" default='""'>
  Authentication password.
</ParamField>

## Event Handlers

| Event       | Description                                                       |
| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `connected` | Fired and named here, so not a missing-event despite no on_ prefix. |
| `idle`      | unfired-event: registered and named here, but nothing fires it.   |

The class also fires a `dropped` event the page never names in a table
(missing-event; a backticked prose mention doesn't count).
